WEBVTT

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:03.135 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>Guide 1. Find a cell. Watch how I find a cell.</c>

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:06.745 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>Then you try it yourself. I'm looking for B2.</c>

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:12.215 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>I'll start with the letter B at the top of the table. That tells me which</c>

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:15.455 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>column to follow down. Now I'll find row 2 using the numbers on the left.</c>

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:23.255 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>Where column B and row 2 meet, I've found B2. Look at the number inside it.</c>

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:29.715 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>It says 30. What does that 30 mean? I'll read the label on the same row:</c>

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:36.515 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>Reusable cups. So B2 tells us that the plan includes 30 reusable cups.</c>

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.555 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>Remember: letter first, number second.</c>

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:46.530 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>Now it's your turn. Return to the lesson card, read the cell address it asks for and find that cell.</c>
